{"chunk_id": "ce3271081d0a", "text": "This chapter recounts the early fate of Karna after Kunti secretly sets her divine child afloat in a basket to hide her shame. The infant, protected by the celestial armor and earrings he was born with, drifts through several rivers until reaching the city of Champa. There, the charioteer Adhiratha and his wife Radha\u2014long childless\u2014discover the radiant child and adopt him, naming him Vasusena. Raised as a Suta\u2019s son, Karna grows into a formidable warrior, studies arms under renowned teachers, and becomes the close ally of Duryodhana and rival of Arjuna. Known for extraordinary generosity, he gives freely to Brahmanas during his daily worship of the Sun. This generosity sets the stage for a pivotal moment when Indra, disguised as a Brahmana, approaches Karna to ask for his divine armor and earrings.\nAdhiratha and Radha discover the radiant infant Karna in a river basket, adopt him, and he grows into a famed warrior allied with Duryodhana.\nThemes: hidden lineage, adoption and fate, divine birth, rivalry with Arjuna, generosity and honor", "vector": [0.01938690058887005, -0.01938690058887005, -0.0036791665479540825, -0.009707026183605194, -0.017581257969141006, 0.023351168259978294, -0.03019360452890396, -0.009055365808308125, -0.043091051280498505, -0.01596568338572979, 0.009489806368947029, -0.004999457858502865, 0.007650223094969988, 0.01049444917589426, -0.0063299317844212055, -0.00925900973379612, 0.040049970149993896, -0.026432979851961136, 0.021762745454907417, -0.030546586960554123, -0.0034161265939474106, -0.011261507868766785, -0.009252221323549747, 0.025536946952342987, -0.027831334620714188, 0.0032973343040794134, 0.01935974694788456, -0.025306150317192078, 0.01178419403731823, -0.054875247180461884, -0.0061975629068911076, -0.011824922636151314, -0.012734532356262207, -0.016454428434371948, -0.02479025162756443, 0.011397270485758781, 0.0007865746156312525, -0.017255427315831184, 0.012734532356262207, 0